    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## clarvia.jobs.dispatch.v1\n\n**Purpose:** Lease pending automation jobs from `clarvia.automation_jobs` and dispatch each to the appropriate internal Next.js endpoint by topic. Triggered by an internal webhook kick (from webhook ingress `after()`) and a 1-minute schedule fallback.\n\n**Input contract:**\n- Webhook kick: POST to `/dispatch-kick` (empty body, wake-up signal)\n- Schedule: every 1 minute\n\n**Output contract:** None. Domain endpoints own job completion inside their transaction (§6.4 step 10). n8n only claims and dispatches; it does not call complete_automation_job.\n\n**Job lifecycle (PostgreSQL via clarvia-postgres-automation):**\n- `claim_automation_jobs('n8n-dispatcher', 10)` — lease up to 10 pending jobs\n- `fail_automation_job(job_id, 'n8n-dispatcher', code, msg)` — mark failed, PG schedules retry or dead-letters\n\n**Topic routing (HTTP with HMAC via clarvia-internal-api):**\n- `stripe.event.process` → `/api/internal/automation/stripe/process`\n- `nurture.enrol` → `/api/internal/automation/nurture/enrol`\n- `email.send` → `/api/internal/automation/email/send`\n- `reconciliation.run` → `/api/internal/automation/reconciliation/run`\n- Unknown → dead-letter with `UNKNOWN_TOPIC`\n\n**HMAC (§5.3):** Body for all topic calls is `{\"jobId\":\"<uuid>\",\"worker\":\"n8n-dispatcher\"}`. HMAC is computed once per job in node 02 over the exact bytes sent.\n\n**Completion model:** Domain API endpoints (e.g. processStripeAutomationJob) call completeAutomationJob inside their DB transaction, per §6.4 step 10. On HTTP success the dispatcher does nothing; on HTTP error the dispatcher calls fail_automation_job via PostgreSQL.\n\n**Owner:** Clarvia automation team.\n\n**Env vars:**\n- `CLARVIA_INTERNAL_URL` — base URL for internal API\n- `CLARVIA_INTERNAL_HMAC_SECRET` — HMAC signing secret\n- `CLARVIA_SENTRY_WEBHOOK_URL` — Sentry ingest endpoint",
        "width": 560,
        "height": 660
      },
      "id": "d1e2f3a4-0002-4a00-8000-000000000016",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [60, 20]
    }
